This cheat is the quick command reference only.

## What does this command do:

Full-featured and highly configurable SFTP, HTTP/S, FTP/S and WebDAV server - S3, Google Cloud Storage, Azure Blob

## Installed from

NOTE: the osuosl mirror commands below are DEAD — /pub/sftpgo/ now 404s (apt/yum).
Install from GitHub release .deb/.rpm instead; see the canonical runbook above.

(dead) Fedora: curl -sS "https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/sftpgo/yum/x86_64/sftpgo.repo" | sudo tee /etc/yum.repos.d/sftpgo.repo && sudo dnf install -y sftpgo
(dead) Raspberry Pi: curl -sS https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/sftpgo/apt/gpg.key | sudo tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/sftpgo.asc && echo "deb https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/sftpgo/apt bookworm main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/sftpgo.list && sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y sftpgo
For Mac install using: brew install sftpgo  (still works)

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/bin/sftpgo
For Raspberry Pi run: /usr/bin/sftpgo
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/sftpgo

